notes: verifies = planned lineage only; published ≠ proven. Last Boss owns EVD. No depends_on. No EVD. evidence_status=none. execution_status=blocked_on_tooling. requires_tol is a node field only (TOL-ROO-006 Vitest cataloged, greenfield); do not claim tests can run. Vocabulary: planned lineage only; never covered/passed/done. Archiving an Active live raid once monitoringEndsAt has passed is behavior, not a required clock (UNT-ROO-147 responsibility and algorithm 1, FNC-ROO-137 behavior, REQ-ROO-144): it must happen whether or not an in-memory ticker is running and whether or not the process restarted. The 60-second bot tick (discord-bot/client.js:257-286) has no auto-end (removed in 9237b35, still absent at f38e137; UNT-ROO-147 notes). At f38e137 the end-time check runs only in runPulseOnce (backend/src/api/liveRaid.routes.js:204-216, Active re-check L210, archive call L211), which runs only inside the pulse ticker (startTicker L290-322) armed by armMonitoringSchedule (L327-394), and at boot in resumeLiveRaidMonitoringIfNeeded (L426-435, archive call L431; called from backend/src/index.js:27-32). Both archive through endLiveRaidSessionInternal (L571-684; EndLiveRaidAndArchive, UNT-ROO-143), the same path as officer End Raid. Skips in code: runPulseOnce returns without archiving when the session is missing or not Active (L199-202); the boot path returns when the session is missing or not Active (L419) or has no monitoring schedule (L422-425). Case 1 can be driven through either runner; while the pulse ticker is not running and the process does not restart, nothing reaches case 1 at f38e137. That is the code gap vs REQ-ROO-144 recorded on UNT-ROO-147 and FNC-ROO-137 (Req Guardian ruling A), not a plan defect. While the Discord rate-limit circuit is open, runPulseOnce returns before its end check (L194-197); that only delays archiving until the first pulse after the circuit closes.
